From a90fc442a7cb72768aee11d28ab2888639901e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:02:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the seven stock pages Reaper had deleted stay deleted on
 the 102.10 base

The 40585 rebase's sweep reset files whose Reaper net change looked like zero to
upstream's text, and for seven pages Reaper deletes that re-created them:
Advanced_APPList_Content.asp (app installer), Advanced_AiDisk_webdav.asp and
update_cloudstatus.asp (AiCloud / WebDAV, Phase 1.3), aidisk.asp (AiDisk wizard,
Phase 1.4), AiProtection_Group.asp (AiProtection), Advanced_Smart_Home_Alexa.asp and
Advanced_Smart_Home_IFTTT.asp (Alexa / IFTTT, Phase 1.1). Four of them shipped in
the merged test images; www/Makefile removed the other three at install. The tree
now matches the pre-rebase stack: no file it deleted exists again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
